 ## Overview
-Temporal differential rendering reduces per-frame computational cost by skipping the rendering of screen regions that have not changed since the previous frame [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of redundant ray-marching or shading work in dynamic scenes where only small portions of the volume or camera view update between iterations [G]. Unlike [Reprojection with Temporal Accumulation](8337-reprojection-with-temporal-accumulation.md), which blends historical buffers to reduce noise, this method performs a binary check for change and completely bypasses the rendering pipeline for clean regions [G].
