 ## Background
-Temporal differential rendering originated in the context of voxel-based real-time rendering and console-based graphics. The dirty-brick approach was implemented in the `voxelG` project by mstampfli, leveraging GPU compute shaders for efficient tile-based culling [S1, unofficial]. The dirty-row hashing approach was developed for console canvas rendering in `csRaymarching` by 0gecco, using FNV hashing for efficient row-level change detection [S2, unofficial]. Partial volume rendering updates between visibility passes were explored in procedural volume exploration to refresh occluding data with newly loaded bricks [S3, unofficial]. Anti-flicker freezing heuristics were later applied in differentiable rendering of bitmap primitives to prevent spurious updates in static regions [S4, unofficial].
